Sval: the content classifier bumps its update generation where it picks the engines to rebuild

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 2078831 (mozilla-central da99a869e530, Firefox
161), unchanged. ESR 153 does not carry it.
ContentClassifierService::ProcessListChanges read mEngines under the lock to
choose the features to rebuild, and UpdateFeatures bumped mUpdateGeneration
and the features' versions under a later lock. An older build closure could
run Populate and Prune with its stale snapshot in between and prune an
engine that the newer call had not scheduled for a rebuild, since it still
existed then. ProcessListChanges bumps both under the lock it reads mEngines
with and hands them to UpdateFeatures, which asserts its features are active
in the snapshot where it used to drop the inactive ones.
Drop this patch when the upstream pin reaches Firefox 161.

diff --git a/toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierService.cpp b/toolkit/components/content-classifier/ContentClassifierService.cpp
